  "id": "COMPOUND:223 - PROTEIN:685",
  "verbalization": "Aminosalicylic acid appears to interact with Serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform through multiple indirect pathways. The first pathway links Aminosalicylic acid to 72 kDa type IV collagenase, which is targeted by Quinaldic Acid, and the latter is known to target the serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform. The second pathway connects Aminosalicylic acid to Diacylglycerol kinase gamma, which is targeted by a compound with a complex structure, and this kinase is also known to target the same phosphatase subunit. The third pathway provides a longer chain of evidence, showing that the diacylglycerol kinase gamma is targeted by a compound with a complex molecular structure, and this compound also targets the phosphatase subunit. These findings suggest that Aminosalicylic acid may exert its effects through a mechanism involving the regulation of serine/threonine-protein phosphatase 2A catalytic subunit beta isoform, possibly through the modulation of downstream signaling pathways. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
